<div style="background-color: #1a5276; color: white; padding: 15px; text-align: center; border-radius: 8px;">
    <h1 style="margin: 0;">Lesson Planner – Theme # 2 – Lesson # 2</h1>
    <p style="margin: 5px 0 0 0; font-size: 1.1em;">Complete this planner five times per theme, once per lesson (Lesson 1 through Lesson 5).</p>
</div>

<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 50%;"><b>Lesson #:</b> 2</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 50%;"><b>Skills Focus:</b> Reading</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Grade:</b> 6th Grade (CEFR: A2.1)</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Scenario:</b> The Talents Around Us</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Theme:</b> Who Will Perform in the Fiestas Patrias Activities?</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Date(s):</b> From ___ to ___</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="2"><b>Learning Sequence Time:</b> 45–50 min</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="3">
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Specific Objective:</b> Reading: reading_1: Create written reflections on stories read in class. reading_2: Analyze characters' actions and motives in stories. phonemic_awareness: Demonstrate knowledge of phonemic awareness by distinguishing spoken rhyming words from non-rhyming words.</p>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Learning Outcome:</b> Reading: Can write reflections on stories about Panamanian traditions and Fiestas Patrias (e.g., 'The girl felt proud wearing the traditional pollera dress in the parade.' 'The boy enjoyed playing the drums for the school band.'). Can analyze characters' actions and motives in stories about Fiestas Patrias celebrations (e.g., 'Liz practiced the traditional dance to perform in the parade.' 'Liz was chosen as the abanderada to lead the parade because she earned the top honor roll for being the best student in the class.'). Can distinguish rhyming words from non-rhyming words in simple comparisons (e.g., 'drum' and 'hum' vs. 'march' and 'flag').</p>
        </td>
    </tr>
</table>

<h2 style="color: #1a5276;">The Six Action-Oriented Approach (AOA) Lesson Stages</h2>

<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <thead style="background-color: #f2f2f2;">
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 33%;">Stage & Description</th>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 33%;">Activities & Teacher Actions</th>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 33%;">Estimated Date and Time</th>
        </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 1 — Warm-up / Pre-task</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(Engagement, Modeling and Clarification)</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Warm-up:</b> The teacher displays a large picture of a Fiestas Patrias parade in Panama, showing students in traditional costumes, a school band, and an 'abanderado' carrying the flag. The teacher asks, "What do you see in the picture?" "What are these students doing?" "Do you know any of these talents?" (e.g., 'playing drums,' 'dancing,' 'twirling the baton'). Students share their initial thoughts, activating vocabulary from Lesson 1 like 'parade,' 'flag,' 'band,' 'costume,' 'dance,' 'perform.'</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Modeling:</b> The teacher points to a student in the picture and says, "Look, this boy is playing the drums. He is very talented. He will play in the parade next week." The teacher models the pronunciation of 'drum' and 'hum' and then 'march' and 'flag', emphasizing the short vowel sounds and demonstrating how to distinguish rhyming from non-rhyming words. The teacher also uses the modal 'can' to describe abilities, "He can play the drums very well."</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Clarification (CCQs):</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Is 'drum' and 'hum' a rhyming pair?" (Expected answer: "Yes!")</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Can everyone play the drums?" (Expected answer: "No, only talented people can play.")</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">[5-7 min]</td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 2 — Presentation</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(Input of new language/content connected to Scenario)</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Material:</b> The teacher presents a short narrative text titled "The Big Fiestas Patrias Show." The text describes a school preparing for the Panamanian National Holidays, focusing on a few students and their talents, their practice, and their plans. It incorporates vocabulary like 'parade,' 'band,' 'flute,' 'drums,' 'accordion,' 'dance,' 'costume,' 'performer,' 'stage,' 'practice,' 'celebrate,' 'talented,' 'excited.' It also features future simple for plans (e.g., 'Liz will dance the traditional dance.') and first conditional for possibilities (e.g., 'If she practices every day, she will perform beautifully.').</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Competence:</b> Interprets and understands written texts to extract specific information about events and character actions.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Comprehension tasks:</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Gist questions:</b> The teacher asks students to read the text silently. "What is the story about?" "Who are the main characters?" (Expected answers: "The school is preparing for Fiestas Patrias," "Liz and Mario are main characters.")</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>True/False statements:</b> Students read the text again and mark statements as True or False (e.g., "Liz will play the drums." "Mario can dance the traditional dance." "The students are nervous about the show."). The teacher checks answers orally.</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">[10-12 min]</td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 3 — Preparation / Practice</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(Accuracy focus on Reading)</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Skill & Content:</b> Reading comprehension, analyzing character actions and motives, future simple for plans, first conditional for possibilities, modal 'can' for ability, target vocabulary, and distinguishing rhyming words.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Detailed Procedure:</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>1. Controlled practice (Sentence Completion & Rhyming):</b> Students receive a worksheet with sentences from the story, but with key vocabulary words (e.g., 'parade,' 'flute,' 'dance,' 'talented') or verbs in future simple/conditional forms missing. They complete the sentences based on the reading text. Example: "If Mario practices his ______, he will play well in the ______." Additionally, they identify and circle rhyming words from a list based on the text (e.g., 'drum' and 'hum' vs. 'stage' and 'flag').</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>2. Semi-controlled (Character Action & Motive Analysis):</b> Students are given prompts to analyze characters' actions and motives. For example, "Why did Liz practice the traditional dance every day?" (Motive: She wanted to perform beautifully in the Fiestas Patrias activities.) "What will Mario do if he practices his accordion a lot?" (Action: He will perform beautifully on stage.) Students write short answers based on the text. The teacher emphasizes using future simple and first conditional constructions.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>3. Pair interaction/Peer check (Reading and Discussion):</b> In pairs, students re-read sections of the story, focusing on sentences with 'can,' 'will,' and 'if...will'. They take turns asking and answering questions about the text, such as "What talent can Liz show?" (She can dance.) or "What will happen if the band practices a lot?" (They will perform an amazing show.). They also check each other's answers for the sentence completion and character analysis tasks.</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">[15-18 min]</td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 4 — Performance / Production</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(Communicative task where students USE the language in a realistic scenario)</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Task format:</b> Individual written reflection on the story's characters.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Students will write a short reflection (3-4 sentences) about one character from "The Big Fiestas Patrias Show." They choose either Liz or Mario and analyze their actions and motivations, expressing their own thoughts about the character's journey. They should include what the character can do, what they will do (their plans), and use a first conditional sentence to describe a possibility for the character. Students are encouraged to use target vocabulary (e.g., 'talented,' 'practice,' 'perform,' 'excited,' 'patriotic').</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Example prompt:</b> "Choose Liz or Mario. Write about their talent and what they will do for the Fiestas Patrias activities. What do you think about their actions? If they practice more, what will happen?"</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Teacher action:</b> The teacher circulates, offering support, checking for use of target grammar and vocabulary, and prompting students to expand their ideas.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">[10 min]</td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 5 — Assessment / Post-task</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(Formative assessment strategy)</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Assessment Task:</b> Students submit their written reflections from the Production stage.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Evaluation Criteria (Teacher Observation/Checklist):</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Analysis of character's actions and motives (e.g., 'Liz practiced the traditional dance to perform in the parade.').</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Use of future simple (e.g., 'She will perform beautifully.').</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Use of first conditional (e.g., 'If she practices, she will do great.').</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Use of modal 'can' (e.g., 'She can dance.').</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Inclusion of relevant vocabulary from the theme (e.g., 'talented,' 'parade,' 'costume,' 'practice').</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Clarity and coherence of written reflection.</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student Self-Assessment / Exit Ticket:</b> Students answer the following questions on a small slip of paper:</p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What is one new thing I learned about Fiestas Patrias talents today?"</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Can I analyze a character's actions in a story?" (Yes/No/A little)</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">[5 min]</td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 6 — Reflection</h3>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student self-reflection prompt:</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"How did reading the story help me understand about preparing for Fiestas Patrias?"</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What was easy or difficult when analyzing the characters' actions?"</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Teacher reflection:</b></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">"The reading activities effectively engaged students with the theme. The use of pictures and the narrative text provided good context for the target vocabulary and grammar. Students generally grasped the concept of future plans and abilities. Some students needed more guidance with the first conditional sentence structure in their reflections. The phonemic awareness activity for rhyming words was quick and effective. For the next lesson, I will ensure more explicit modeling for constructing conditional sentences and provide sentence starters for written reflections to further support their writing output."</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Connection to next lesson in the theme sequence:</b></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">"This lesson’s focus on reading about talents and Fiestas Patrias performances, as well as analyzing character actions and plans, will directly prepare students for Lesson 3 (Speaking & Interaction). In the next lesson, students will use this vocabulary and grammar to talk about their own or their classmates' talents and plans for Fiestas Patrias, describing abilities and discussing future performance possibilities in interactive speaking tasks."</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">[3-5 min]</td>
        </tr>
    </tbody>
</table>